   "source": [
    "FEATS = ['n_uteis', 'lag1_media', 'lag2_media', 'lag3_media', 'mm3_media', 'mes_sin', 'mes_cos',\n",
    "         'mes_sin2', 'mes_cos2', 'segundo_semestre', 'fim_trimestre', 'fim_semestre']\n",
    "\n",
    "def serie_mensal(target, tab=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Serie mensal do TOTAL (index datetime freq MS). target in {'valor','qntd'}.\n",
    "    tab: tab_mensal-like DataFrame p/ usar no lugar do global `tab_mensal` -- usado pela\n",
    "    Secao de estratos (CIA/Canal/Canal-NE) p/ rodar o mesmo motor de walk-forward por estrato.\"\"\"\n",
    "    _tab = tab_mensal if tab is None else tab\n",
    "    _col = 'tot_valor' if target == 'valor' else 'tot_qntd'\n",
    "    s = _tab.set_index('periodo')[_col].astype(float)\n",
    "    s.index = pd.DatetimeIndex(s.index).to_period('M').to_timestamp()\n",
    "    return s.asfreq('MS')\n",
    "\n",
    "def montar_tabela(target, tab=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Tabela supervisionada 1-linha-por-mes. Alvo = media por dia util (col 'media').\n",
    "       Reconstrucao do total = media x n_uteis. Retorna tab_sup (linhas com lags validos).\n",
    "       tab: tab_mensal-like DataFrame p/ usar no lugar do global `tab_mensal` (estratos).\"\"\"\n",
    "    _tab = tab_mensal if tab is None else tab\n",
    "    _mcol = 'media_valor' if target == 'valor' else 'media_qntd'\n",
    "    _tcol = 'tot_valor'   if target == 'valor' else 'tot_qntd'\n",
    "    t = _tab.copy()\n",
    "    t['media'] = t[_mcol].astype(float)\n",
    "    t['tot']   = t[_tcol].astype(float)\n",
    "    for _k in (1, 2, 3):\n",
    "        t[f'lag{_k}_media'] = t['media'].shift(_k)\n",
    "    t['mm3_media'] = t['media'].shift(1).rolling(3, min_periods=1).mean()   # so passado (shift antes)\n",
    "    _m = t['periodo'].dt.month\n",
    "    t['mes_sin'] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * _m / 12.0)\n",
    "    t['mes_cos'] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * _m / 12.0)\n",
    "    t['mes_sin2'] = np.sin(4 * np.pi * _m / 12.0)   # 2o harmonico -- ciclo semestral (6 meses)\n",
    "    t['mes_cos2'] = np.cos(4 * np.pi * _m / 12.0)\n",
    "    t['segundo_semestre'] = (_m > 6).astype(int)    # 0 = jan-jun, 1 = jul-dez\n",
    "    t['fim_trimestre'] = _m.isin([3, 6, 9, 12]).astype(int)\n",
    "    t['fim_semestre']  = _m.isin([6, 12]).astype(int)\n",
    "    tab_sup = t.dropna(subset=FEATS).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    return tab_sup\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Exemplo VALOR:')\n",
    "_ex = montar_tabela('valor')\n",
    "print(f'  serie_m: {len(serie_mensal(\"valor\"))} meses | tab_sup: {len(_ex)} linhas usaveis '\n",
    "      f'({_ex[\"periodo\"].min().date()} -> {_ex[\"periodo\"].max().date()})')\n",
    "_ex[['periodo', 'n_uteis', 'media', 'lag1_media', 'lag2_media', 'lag3_media', 'mm3_media', 'tot']]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "30219cac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "###  4.1 - Series observadas + medias moveis (MM3/MM6/MM12/MM24)\n",
    "\n",
    "Antes de qualquer decomposicao formal, o jeito mais simples de enxergar tendencia \"no olho\" e\n",
    "sobrepor medias moveis **centradas** de janelas diferentes na serie mensal bruta (`tot_valor`/\n",
    "`tot_qntd`, Secao 3): janelas curtas (MM3) acompanham de perto a serie e suavizam so o ruido\n",
    "mes a mes; janelas longas (MM12, MM24) filtram ate a sazonalidade e mostram so o nivel de longo\n",
    "prazo. Onde as curvas mais longas mudam de inclinacao e um bom indicio visual de quebra de\n",
    "regime -- para comparar com o diagnostico formal ja feito na Secao 2.6."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "37f83741",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1300x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
